{"name":"Golden Promise","hex":"#ffc64d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"promise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oath or affirmation; a vow.","A transaction between two persons whereby the first person undertakes in the future to render some service or gift to the second person or devotes something valuable now and here to their use."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To commit to (some action or outcome), or to assure (a person) of such commitment; to make an oath or vow.","To give grounds for expectation, especially of something good."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Promise","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Promise is a variety of spring-sown two-row barley. It was developed in the 1950s by exposing an existing variety to gamma radiation with the aim of producing a semi-dwarf variety of barley that had good malting characteristics. It became very popular with farmers during the 1970s but began to be replaced by higher yielding varieties in the 1980s. Due to its perceived better flavour than these more modern varieties, a niche market was maintained and it is still favoured by craft brewers. It has been used by researchers to study the genetics of barley and to investigate the effect of barley on the flavour of beer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Promise","wikidata":"Q119039784"},{"title":"Promise","blocks":[{"text":"A promise is a commitment by someone to do or not do something. As a noun promise means a declaration assuring that one will or will not do something. As a verb it means to commit oneself by a promise to do or give. It can also mean a capacity for good, similar to a value that is to be realized in the near future."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promise","wikidata":"Q1425577"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/500px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/1280px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg/500px-Immigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American immigrants seen swearing the Oath of Allegiance in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImmigrants_to_the_United_States_take_the_Oath_of_Allegiance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg/500px-William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/William_Holman_Hunt_-_Rienzi_vowing_to_obtain_justice.jp